  "body": "### Summary\nAs a Mac session, I want a stable hosted test of tapping the already-selected sidebar row (iPad / unfolded Duo), so that #426's re-selection on the split root is guarded by CI and not only by a hand check.\n\n### Scope\n- w426 wrote a hosted test that calls the sidebar `UICollectionView` delegate's `didSelectItemAt` on the selected row (PR #1318). It passes when run alone: the haptic plays and the selection is kept.\n- It fails in every combined run: after other hosted suites have run in the same test process, the sidebar collection view shows one section and one item.\n- Find the leak (shared window or scene state, `UIHostingController` reuse, list-style caching), isolate the test, and ship it.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1318\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The test passes alone and inside the full app test run, and fails if `RootModel.selectFromSidebar` stops treating a same-row tap as a re-selection.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
